Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (C) 2026 Shepherd Research Lab, University of Hawaiʻi Cancer Center

Beginning in 2025, this repository was extended into a federated-learning
training and evaluation system for breast cancer detection across multiple
clinical sites, built on NVIDIA FLARE (NVFLARE). The additions include:

  - Federated methods: FedAvg, FedProx, FedBN, and personalized Ditto
    (scalar and module-wise), implemented as an NVFLARE executor.
  - Crash-resume of interrupted federated runs.
  - Optional per-site precision and micro-batch controls for training on
    memory-constrained GPUs.
  - Post-hoc per-subgroup (race/ethnicity) fairness analysis tooling.

These modifications are described in:

  Sollis LJ, Young PM, Bunnell A, Quon B, Hernandez BY, Wolfgruber TK,
  Shepherd J. "Personalized Federated Learning for Equitable Breast Cancer
  Detection in Underrepresented Pacific Islander Populations." Presented at
  the MICCAI 2026 Workshop on Distributed, Collaborative, and Federated
  Learning (DeCaF); to appear in Springer Lecture Notes in Computer Science.

